# Project recovery handoff

`PROJECT-RECOVERY.md` is the repository handoff. The runtime baseline SHA there is the last verified application/runtime commit. It is not necessarily the current GitHub `main` tip. Documentation-only commits do not move that baseline.

Before substantial work:

- Read `PROJECT-RECOVERY.md`.
- `git fetch origin main` and compare `git rev-parse origin/main` with the stored runtime baseline.
- If a PR recorded in the handoff has merged, reconcile the document against `origin/main`.
- Never assume the stored SHA is the current `main` tip.
- Do not follow a stale pin or behavior note when the repo disagrees. Correct the document in the PR you are already making when the correction matters.

Before a significant Cursor-managed PR is considered complete, update `PROJECT-RECOVERY.md` in that same PR:

- Record the feature or fix.
- Record the PR number if it is available.
- Record the tested branch and head SHA.
- Record tests and status.
- Update pins, behavior, and future work when those changed.
- Move the runtime baseline only when application or runtime behavior changed.

Do not open a follow-up documentation PR solely to record a merge. The next session verifies the merge and reconciles `origin/main`.

Do not update `PROJECT-RECOVERY.md` for trivial formatting-only edits.

Never put secrets, tokens, passwords, `.env` contents, service-role keys, or other private credentials in `PROJECT-RECOVERY.md`. Public domains and project refs already visible in the repository may stay.

Incident rollback stays in `STAGE11_RECOVERY.md` and `docs/EMERGENCY.md`. Do not copy secret values out of those procedures.
